## Coding Standards

### TypeScript/JavaScript
- Follow strict TypeScript typing
- Use ESLint with Airbnb style guide
- Implement Prettier for code formatting
- Write comprehensive JSDoc comments
- Use functional programming patterns where appropriate

### Python (FastAPI)
- Follow PEP 8 coding standards
- Use type hints throughout
- Implement proper error handling
- Write unit tests with pytest
- Document API endpoints with OpenAPI specifications

### React/Next.js
- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement component-based architecture
- Follow atomic design principles
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Implement proper state management

### Database
- Use Prisma ORM for type-safe database operations
- Follow database normalization principles
- Implement proper indexing strategies
- Use transactions for data consistency

### Security
- All API endpoints require authentication
- Implement proper input validation and sanitization
- Use HTTPS in production environments
- Regular security audits and updates

### Testing
- Unit tests for all business logic
- Integration tests for API endpoints
- End-to-end tests for critical user flows
- Test coverage should be maintained above 80%

### Documentation
- Maintain up-to-date API documentation
- Document all public APIs with examples
- Keep README files updated with current information
- Provide code comments for complex logic

